## Name resolution: collects declarations, resolves imports, and lowers declaration contents to
## HIR, where every name points to its definition. Follows `resolve.rs`, `lower.rs` and
## `builtins.rs` of the reference implementation (emela-resolve), which call each other; modules
## cannot, so both are here.
##
## Three phases:
##
## 1. Collect declarations: per module, register definitions in separate namespaces (types,
##    constructors, values)
## 2. Imports: once every module's declarations are in, bring the listed names and modules into
##    scope
## 3. Lower: turn declaration contents (types, expressions, patterns) into HIR
##
## The built-in modules of the reference are always empty in `emela check` (`NoBuiltins`), so they
## are left out.
